WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:06.490
The tumultuous arrest of women's rights activist
Emmeline Pankhurst outside Buckingham Palace

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:17.920
- and Emily Davison throwing herself
in front of the horses at the Kings Derby - 
 iconic Images from 1913.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:29.070
The struggle for womens suffrage in Europe is just heating up. In Germany activists like Helene Lange and
Clara Zetkin were a driving force to get the

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:33.210
vote - in a country where a women were banned
from even attending political gatherings until

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.940
1908.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:43.620
From 1914 external factors shaped the role
of women in society.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.820
Many say that women's contribution to the
war effort back home helped secure them the

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.870
vote in 1918 in Britain...

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:54.869
And in Germany.

00:00:54.869 --> 00:01:00.260
After the revolution - women thronged to the
streets to vote for the first time in elections

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:05.850
to the Weimar National Assembly in January
1919.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:13.200
Latecomers to the table of womens' suffrage
were Spain in 1931, France in 1944 and Italy

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.810
in 1945.

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:19.909
And in Portugal women were barred from voting
in national politics until as recently as

00:01:19.909 --> 00:01:23.689
1976...

00:01:23.689 --> 00:01:28.689
And although it's not uncommon to see women
at the helm in European politics today...

00:01:28.689 --> 00:08:21.219
take a wider view - and you'll see the struggle
for total equality is stilll far from over.

